<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn2:definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bpmn2="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:bioc="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn/biocolor/1.0" xmlns:color="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/non-normative/color/1.0" id="secure-container-release-combined" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL BPMN20.xsd">
  <bpmn2:collaboration id="Collaboration_SCRCombined">
    <bpmn2:documentation>The secure container release chain as one process with three lanes: ocean carrier, secure release provider and rights holder. A task sits where the initiative lies, the provider applying it to the record is a side effect, and every state box sits in the provider's lane. The carrier's intervention window runs in parallel with the whole chain, and a revocation terminates everything. The terminal has no lane: it verifies the pickup rights at the gate back-to-back with the provider, under the hood, and no state changes hands. The black-box pools are the processes it hooks into; the message flows mirror the ones drawn in those processes' own BPMNs.</bpmn2:documentation>
    <bpmn2:participant id="Participant_SCRCombined" name="Secure container release" processRef="Process_SCRCombined" />
    <bpmn2:participant id="Participant_Agency" name="Import agency at destination" />
    <bpmn2:participant id="Participant_Transport" name="Container import transport" />
    <bpmn2:messageFlow id="Obs_AssignedToAgency" name="Container release right [pickup rights assigned]" sourceRef="Task_P2_AssignRights" targetRef="Participant_Agency" />
    <bpmn2:messageFlow id="Obs_AssignedToTransport" name="Container release right [pickup rights assigned]" sourceRef="Task_P2_AssignRights" targetRef="Participant_Transport" />
    <bpmn2:messageFlow id="Obs_PickupAssigned" name="Container import [pickup assigned]" sourceRef="Participant_Transport" targetRef="Task_P2_Transfer" />
  </bpmn2:collaboration>
  <bpmn2:process id="Process_SCRCombined" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn2:laneSet id="LaneSet_SCRCombined">
      <bpmn2:lane id="Lane_Carrier" name="Ocean carrier">
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_P1</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Task_P1_Register</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Task_P1_Release</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Split</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Gateway_P1_Intervention</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Task_P1_Intervene</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Gateway_P1_Revoked</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_P1_Revoked</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_P1_Spent</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn2:lane>
      <bpmn2:lane id="Lane_Provider" name="Secure release provider">
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Task_P2_AssignRights</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn2:lane>
      <bpmn2:lane id="Lane_Holder" name="Rights holder">
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Gateway_P2_Transfer</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Task_P2_Transfer</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Gateway_P2_Join</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>Task_P2_Assign</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn2:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_P2_Ready</bpmn2:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn2:lane>
    </bpmn2:laneSet>
    <bpmn2:startEvent id="StartEvent_P1" name="Import container announced">
      <bpmn2:documentation>The carrier knows the container is inbound and can open a release record against it. The release conditions are not necessarily met yet - that is what separates registration from the factual release.</bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:startEvent>
    <bpmn2:task id="Task_P1_Register" name="Register container release&#10;(B/L, container, first rights holder)">
      <bpmn2:documentation>The carrier names the first rights holder: its own nominated haulier under carrier haulage, or the consignee / forwarder under merchant haulage. Replaces the release PIN that used to be e-mailed onward. The record now exists but the right is not yet exercisable.</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation id="DataOut_Task_P1_Register">
        <bpmn2:targetRef>DataRef_Task_P1_Register</bpmn2:targetRef>
      </bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn2:task>
    <bpmn2:task id="Task_P1_Release" name="Release container">
      <bpmn2:documentation>The factual release, and a separate act from creating the record. Bill of lading surrendered, freight and demurrage settled, no customs or carrier hold outstanding. It can follow registration by days or coincide with it, but only from here is the right exercisable by its holder.</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation id="DataOut_Task_P1_Release">
        <bpmn2:targetRef>DataRef_Task_P1_Release</bpmn2:targetRef>
      </bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn2:task>
    <bpmn2:parallelGateway id="Gateway_Split">
      <bpmn2:documentation>From the release onward two things run side by side: the release chain towards the gate, and the carrier's intervention window, which stays open for as long as the right is live.</bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn2:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_P1_Intervention" name="Carrier intervention?" default="Flow_P1_NoIntervention" />
    <bpmn2:task id="Task_P1_Intervene" name="Block / unblock / revoke&#10;release right">
      <bpmn2:documentation>Raised for unpaid demurrage, a fraud signal, a commercial dispute or a corrected B/L. The provider validates that the requester is the issuing carrier and pushes the resulting state to every party currently authorised to see the right - neither of which is a step of its own. Available for the whole lifetime of the release, which is why this branch loops.</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation id="DataOut_Task_P1_Intervene">
        <bpmn2:targetRef>DataRef_Task_P1_Intervene</bpmn2:targetRef>
      </bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn2:task>
    <bpmn2:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_P1_Revoked" name="Revoked?" default="Flow_P1_NotRevoked" />
    <bpmn2:endEvent id="EndEvent_P1_Revoked" name="Release right revoked">
      <bpmn2:documentation>Terminates the whole process, not only this branch: a revoked right cannot be picked up, so any step still pending in the release chain ends with it.</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:terminateEventDefinition id="Terminate_EndEvent_P1_Revoked" />
    </bpmn2:endEvent>
    <bpmn2:endEvent id="EndEvent_P1_Spent" name="Carrier control spent">
      <bpmn2:documentation>Not an action by either party. The carrier's intervention window closes when the right can no longer be moved - the container picked up, or the right revoked. What happens to the record afterwards is the provider's own business and has no bilateral agreement; see the lifecycle note.</bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:endEvent>
    <bpmn2:task id="Task_P2_AssignRights" name="Assign pickup rights">
      <bpmn2:documentation>The provider's own act, once the carrier has released the container - and its only step. It assigns the pickup rights to the first rights holder: the forwarder acting as the consignee's agent, or the consignee itself. Assigned, not offered: there is no acceptance. Only the data the holder needs in order to act, not the commercial terms behind the release (design principle 8).</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation id="DataOut_Task_P2_AssignRights">
        <bpmn2:targetRef>DataRef_Task_P2_AssignRights</bpmn2:targetRef>
      </bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn2:task>
    <bpmn2:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_P2_Transfer" name="Onward transfer?" default="Flow_P2_NoTransfer" />
    <bpmn2:task id="Task_P2_Transfer" name="Transfer / revoke&#10;release right">
      <bpmn2:documentation>Carrier haulage: the carrier-appointed haulier transfers to a subcontractor. Merchant haulage: the consignee or forwarder appoints a trucking company. The provider checks that the transferring party is the current holder, re-registers the right and withdraws the previous holder's access - all consequences of this act, not steps beside it. No token changes hands because there is no token. Repeats for every step in the chain, and the holder can revoke a transfer it made.</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation id="DataOut_Task_P2_Transfer">
        <bpmn2:targetRef>DataRef_Task_P2_Transfer</bpmn2:targetRef>
      </bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation>
      <bpmn2:standardLoopCharacteristics />
    </bpmn2:task>
    <bpmn2:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_P2_Join" />
    <bpmn2:task id="Task_P2_Assign" name="Nominate&#10;representative">
      <bpmn2:documentation>The last rights holder in the chain nominates its representative for the pickup: a concrete driver identity and licence plate. The representative never receives a code: the right stays with the provider, and the terminal verifies it against the driver at the gate, under the hood. Can be renominated until the driver is at the gate.</bpmn2:documentation>
      <bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation id="DataOut_Task_P2_Assign">
        <bpmn2:targetRef>DataRef_Task_P2_Assign</bpmn2:targetRef>
      </bpmn2:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn2:task>
    <bpmn2:endEvent id="EndEvent_P2_Ready" name="Pickup ready">
      <bpmn2:documentation>The chain's last state is representative nominated. At the gate the terminal verifies the pickup rights back-to-back with the provider, under the hood: no state changes hands, so no step follows.</bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:endEvent>
    <bpmn2:dataObjectReference id="DataRef_Task_P1_Register" name="Container release right&#10;[registered]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Right">
      <bpmn2:dataState id="State_Task_P1_Register" name="registered" />
    </bpmn2:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn2:dataObjectReference id="DataRef_Task_P1_Release" name="Container release right&#10;[released]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Right">
      <bpmn2:dataState id="State_Task_P1_Release" name="released" />
    </bpmn2:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn2:dataObjectReference id="DataRef_Task_P1_Intervene" name="Container release right&#10;[blocked / revoked]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Right">
      <bpmn2:dataState id="State_Task_P1_Intervene" name="blocked / revoked" />
    </bpmn2:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn2:dataObjectReference id="DataRef_Task_P2_AssignRights" name="Container release right&#10;[pickup rights assigned]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Right">
      <bpmn2:dataState id="State_Task_P2_AssignRights" name="pickup rights assigned" />
    </bpmn2:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn2:dataObjectReference id="DataRef_Task_P2_Transfer" name="Container release right&#10;[transferred]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Right">
      <bpmn2:dataState id="State_Task_P2_Transfer" name="transferred" />
    </bpmn2:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn2:dataObjectReference id="DataRef_Task_P2_Assign" name="Container release right&#10;[representative nominated]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Right">
      <bpmn2:dataState id="State_Task_P2_Assign" name="representative nominated" />
    </bpmn2:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn2:dataObject id="DataObject_Right" name="Container release right" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_01" sourceRef="StartEvent_P1" targetRef="Task_P1_Register" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_02" sourceRef="Task_P1_Register" targetRef="Task_P1_Release" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_03" sourceRef="Task_P1_Release" targetRef="Gateway_Split" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Split_Carrier" sourceRef="Gateway_Split" targetRef="Gateway_P1_Intervention" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Split_Chain" sourceRef="Gateway_Split" targetRef="Task_P2_AssignRights" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_04" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_P1_Intervention" targetRef="Task_P1_Intervene" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_NoIntervention" name="No" sourceRef="Gateway_P1_Intervention" targetRef="EndEvent_P1_Spent" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_05" sourceRef="Task_P1_Intervene" targetRef="Gateway_P1_Revoked" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_06" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_P1_Revoked" targetRef="EndEvent_P1_Revoked" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P1_NotRevoked" name="No" sourceRef="Gateway_P1_Revoked" targetRef="Gateway_P1_Intervention" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2_03" sourceRef="Task_P2_AssignRights" targetRef="Gateway_P2_Transfer" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2_04" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_P2_Transfer" targetRef="Task_P2_Transfer" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2_NoTransfer" name="No" sourceRef="Gateway_P2_Transfer" targetRef="Gateway_P2_Join" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2_05" sourceRef="Task_P2_Transfer" targetRef="Gateway_P2_Join" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2_06" sourceRef="Gateway_P2_Join" targetRef="Task_P2_Assign" />
    <bpmn2:sequenceFlow id="Flow_P2_07" sourceRef="Task_P2_Assign" targetRef="EndEvent_P2_Ready" />
    <bpmn2:textAnnotation id="Anno_P1_Release">
      <bpmn2:text>Registration and release are two acts, not one. The record can sit registered and unusable while a hold, an unpaid invoice or an unsurrendered B/L stands.</bpmn2:text>
    </bpmn2:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn2:association id="Assoc_Anno_P1_Release" sourceRef="Task_P1_Release" targetRef="Anno_P1_Release" />
    <bpmn2:textAnnotation id="Anno_P1_Window">
      <bpmn2:text>Carrier control survives release and runs in parallel with the whole release chain, until the container is picked up or the right revoked - which is why it loops rather than running to a finish.</bpmn2:text>
    </bpmn2:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn2:association id="Assoc_Anno_P1_Window" sourceRef="EndEvent_P1_Spent" targetRef="Anno_P1_Window" />
    <bpmn2:textAnnotation id="Anno_P2_1">
      <bpmn2:text>The receiving party becomes the rights holder and these steps repeat with it. A third-party rights holder is therefore not a separate lane.</bpmn2:text>
    </bpmn2:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn2:association id="Assoc_Anno_P2_1" sourceRef="Task_P2_Transfer" targetRef="Anno_P2_1" />
    <bpmn2:textAnnotation id="Anno_Legend">
      <bpmn2:text>Legend. One process, three lanes. Lanes show initiative, not work - a task sits with the party that takes the action, and the provider applying it to the record is a side effect that is not drawn. Every step produces a state, and every state box sits in the provider's lane because the provider holds it: states the carrier causes on the upper row, the rest on the lower row. At the gate the terminal verifies the pickup rights back-to-back with the provider, under the hood: no state changes hands, so there is no terminal lane.</bpmn2:text>
    </bpmn2:textAnnotation>
  </bpmn2:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_SCRCombined">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_SCRCombined" bpmnElement="Collaboration_SCRCombined">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_SCRCombined" bpmnElement="Participant_SCRCombined" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2260" height="840" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Carrier" bpmnElement="Lane_Carrier" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="2230" height="260" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Provider" bpmnElement="Lane_Provider" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="340" width="2230" height="300" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Holder" bpmnElement="Lane_Holder" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="640" width="2230" height="280" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_StartEvent_P1" bpmnElement="StartEvent_P1">
        <dc:Bounds x="282" y="222" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="248" y="265" width="104" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_P1_Register" bpmnElement="Task_P1_Register">
        <dc:Bounds x="420" y="200" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_P1_Release" bpmnElement="Task_P1_Release">
        <dc:Bounds x="600" y="200" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gateway_Split" bpmnElement="Gateway_Split">
        <dc:Bounds x="815" y="215" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gateway_P1_Intervention" bpmnElement="Gateway_P1_Intervention" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="995" y="215" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="895" y="183" width="95" height="28" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_P1_Intervene" bpmnElement="Task_P1_Intervene">
        <dc:Bounds x="1140" y="200" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gateway_P1_Revoked" bpmnElement="Gateway_P1_Revoked" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1355" y="215" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1335" y="177" width="90" height="28" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_EndEvent_P1_Revoked" bpmnElement="EndEvent_P1_Revoked">
        <dc:Bounds x="1542" y="222" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1508" y="265" width="104" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_EndEvent_P1_Spent" bpmnElement="EndEvent_P1_Spent">
        <dc:Bounds x="1722" y="222" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1688" y="265" width="104" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_P2_AssignRights" bpmnElement="Task_P2_AssignRights">
        <dc:Bounds x="780" y="450" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gateway_P2_Transfer" bpmnElement="Gateway_P2_Transfer" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="995" y="695" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="975" y="657" width="90" height="28" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_P2_Transfer" bpmnElement="Task_P2_Transfer">
        <dc:Bounds x="1140" y="680" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Gateway_P2_Join" bpmnElement="Gateway_P2_Join" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1355" y="695" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_P2_Assign" bpmnElement="Task_P2_Assign">
        <dc:Bounds x="1500" y="680" width="120" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_EndEvent_P2_Ready" bpmnElement="EndEvent_P2_Ready">
        <dc:Bounds x="1722" y="702" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1688" y="745" width="104" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_DataRef_Task_P1_Register" bpmnElement="DataRef_Task_P1_Register">
        <dc:Bounds x="428" y="360" width="36" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="468" y="368" width="70" height="34" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_DataRef_Task_P1_Release" bpmnElement="DataRef_Task_P1_Release">
        <dc:Bounds x="608" y="360" width="36" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="648" y="368" width="70" height="34" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_DataRef_Task_P1_Intervene" bpmnElement="DataRef_Task_P1_Intervene">
        <dc:Bounds x="1148" y="360" width="36" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1188" y="368" width="70" height="34" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_DataRef_Task_P2_AssignRights" bpmnElement="DataRef_Task_P2_AssignRights">
        <dc:Bounds x="788" y="570" width="36" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="828" y="578" width="70" height="34" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_DataRef_Task_P2_Transfer" bpmnElement="DataRef_Task_P2_Transfer">
        <dc:Bounds x="1148" y="570" width="36" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1188" y="578" width="70" height="34" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_DataRef_Task_P2_Assign" bpmnElement="DataRef_Task_P2_Assign">
        <dc:Bounds x="1508" y="570" width="36" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1548" y="578" width="70" height="34" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Anno_P1_Release" bpmnElement="Anno_P1_Release">
        <dc:Bounds x="400" y="94" width="320" height="66" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Anno_P1_Window" bpmnElement="Anno_P1_Window">
        <dc:Bounds x="1850" y="190" width="380" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Anno_P2_1" bpmnElement="Anno_P2_1">
        <dc:Bounds x="980" y="825" width="300" height="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Anno_Legend" bpmnElement="Anno_Legend">
        <dc:Bounds x="1850" y="700" width="540" height="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_P1_01" bpmnElement="Flow_P1_01">
        <di:waypoint x="318" y="240" />
        <di:waypoint x="420" y="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_P1_02" bpmnElement="Flow_P1_02">
        <di:waypoint x="540" y="240" />
        <di:waypoint x="600" y="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
